id: pm-stq61b
title: "Unknown-option recovery drops a dash-leading prose value: the advertised replay closes, comments or creates without the user's text"
description: "Found while closing pm-gh1633. Its close reason began with '--unset', and pm close <id> \"--unset accepts ...\" was refused as unknown option '--unset accepts ...'. Commander treats any argv token that starts with '--' as an option, even a quoted multi-word value. The generic unknown-option fallback in resolveUnknownOptionRetry then removes that token and advertises the remainder as 'Replay with suggested correction'. Reproduced on this branch in an isolated tracker:\n\n- pm close <id> \"--unset is now a list\" suggests pm close <id>, which closes with no reason.\n- pm comments <id> \"--flag style comment text\" suggests pm item comments <id>, which drops the comment.\n- pm create \"--weird title\" --type Task suggests pm create --type Task, which drops the title.\n\nThe refusal also calls the prose 'not declared on any command path' and advises a nearest option. A token containing whitespace can never be an option spelling, and pm close <id> -- \"--unset is now a list\" works today. Replaying the advertised command loses user data or performs a different mutation, which breaks the recovery contract that a suggested retry preserves intent."
type: Issue
status: closed
priority: 2
tags[3]: agent-ux,recovery,sdk
created_at: "2026-10-30T13:54:31.173Z"
updated_at: "2026-10-30T13:59:12.537Z"
closed_at: "2026-10-30T13:59:11.659Z"
completed_at: "2026-10-30T13:59:11.659Z"
author: "harness:claude-code"
estimated_minutes: 90
acceptance_criteria: "Never advertise a retry that drops a whitespace-bearing unknown-option token; Offer a -- separator retry only when it preserves the value and all other arguments in order; Explain in the refusal that the value starts with -- and how to pass it, without the declared-nowhere option advice; Cover close, comments and create through SDK and CLI tests, with a pre-fix negative control"
parent: pm-mpbb
risk: medium
confidence: high
severity: medium
resolution: "A whitespace-bearing unknown option is classified as a value. Its replay passes it after a -- separator when only options follow, and otherwise advertises no retry. The refusal explains how to pass the value instead of giving declared-nowhere option advice."
expected_result: "A dash-leading prose value is never dropped by an advertised replay; when safe, the replay passes it after a -- separator, otherwise the refusal explains how to pass it."
actual_result: "close and comments replays preserve and store the text. create with a following --type value advertises no lossy retry. 5 new unit cases fail on the pre-fix source and pass with the fix. The CLI integration replay test, CLI unit suite 843/843 and the refusal-closure gate pass."
component: cli
